From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msvcp60: Throw the object as its own class from _Doraise.

msvcp60 exports _Doraise for its exception classes, and their vtables have
it after what. The VC6 headers' exception::_Raise calls it to throw the
object as its own class (microsoft/STL keeps the same member:
"void _Doraise() const override { _RAISE(*this); }"). Every class shared one
stub that did nothing, so _Raise fell through to throwing the base type.
Each class now has its own _Doraise, which throws a copy of the object with
that class's throw information. The throw information that bad_cast,
logic_error and the msvcp60-only classes lacked is added.

Gate: test/msvcp60-doraise-gate.sh (64/32).
